# Planted probes. Each carries a deliberate defect so a test can prove the gate
# fails on it, and each is deleted again by the test and by `composer
# probes:clean`. Ignored so a copy left behind by a killed run can never be
# committed - this one sits inside the committed demo module, whose tree is
# compared byte for byte, so a stray copy there is worse than elsewhere. The
# host's own two probes are ignored in modules/host/.gitignore. Nothing is
# hidden: the tests still assert each probe is gone, and tools/clean-probes.php
# exits non-zero if one cannot be removed.
/modules/demo/tests/Feature/QaStanProbe.php
# Its neighbour, planted by DeptracBoundaryEnforcementTest: the same argument
# with a sharper edge, because this one declares a module test class importing
# App\Support\ModuleHost\ModuleRegistry, so a committed copy is a boundary
# violation inside the byte-compared demo tree that fails `composer deptrac` at
# the gate's third step.
/modules/demo/tests/Feature/DeptracProbeTest.php
